{"id": "P0", "version": 1, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "TODO: the owner states what this project is for (stub from aec init)"}
// 2026-11-01: Zach's accepted purpose, requirements, direction, assumptions and decisions, carried from Data Guide (archived), anchored to docs/.
{"id": "P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Turn raw or semi-cleaned tabular data into useful, communicable understanding — an enhanced data dictionary, diagnostic EDA engine and repeatable working record — not merely an automatic plot generator; understanding before modeling (assumptions, data-generating process, EDA, usefulness)", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach as DG-P0@2 (2026-11-01 12:39 CT); carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-P0@2", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "P0@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:Fathom turns raw or semi-cleaned tabular datasets into understanding", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Everything else looks good from that batch.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RA", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Separate observations, descriptions, interpretations, hypotheses and recommended actions; attach evidence, confidence/uncertainty and provenance", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RA@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**A.** Separate observations", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Everything else looks good from that batch.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RB", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Never present inferred semantic types or narrative interpretations as known domain facts; overrides and alternative explanations are first-class. This must not block results that rest on an inferred interpretation where they would otherwise be useful: show them, labelled as inferred", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RB@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**B.** Never present inferred", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:DG-RB is correct, provided that it does not entirely block off results", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RC", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The analysis question and variable semantics govern metric and visual selection; avoid all-pairs (Cartesian-cross) explosions of metrics and visuals", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RC@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**C.** Let the analysis question", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:DG-RC should be interpreted as all-pairs Cartesian-Cross explosions", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RD", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Support iterative re-profiling and before/after comparison. Each profile carries its context (snapshot date, source, transformations applied and their types, other recorded changes), and a comparison states those differences first, so what differs from the get-go is visible before the measured deltas", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RD@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**D.** Enable iterative re-profiling", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:I'd like a DG-RD addendum that adds profile context to comparisons", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RE", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "A machine-readable data artifact is the stable interface; stakeholder documents are derived views", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RE@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**E.** Keep a machine-readable data artifact", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Everything else looks good from that batch.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-RF", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Test metric accuracy, degradation on unavailable dependencies, type routing, output reproducibility and preservation of the declared purpose", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-RF@2", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**F.** Test metric accuracy", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Everything else looks good from that batch.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D1", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "Direction: understanding, not only profiling — typed, evidenced findings; inference labelled; unknowns kept as open questions; a machine-readable artifact with derived reports. The MVP is data to decisions, where a decision may be about the data itself, about other processes that turn data into decisions, or the answer to a question", "rationale": "carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-D1@3", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:The MVP here is data -> decisions", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-A1", "version": 1, "type": "assumption", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The output, or a version of it, works standalone as data documentation for most data projects: a fuller data dictionary, readable by a similar audience. Data scientists are a main user, not the only one", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-A1@2", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:capable of standalone functioning as data documentation", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-A2", "version": 1, "type": "assumption", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "No code is fixed; only the guiding documents are. Any component may be removed and rewritten", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-A2@2", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:none of the code is sacred", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-A3", "version": 1, "type": "assumption", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Leave room for an AI-written narrative, possibly through relay-kit. Rule findings stay rule findings; any AI narrative is a separate, labelled layer", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-A3@2", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:leave room for an AI narrative, possibly through RelayKit", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-A4", "version": 1, "type": "assumption", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Without a declared question or intention, usefulness falls back to the general uses of documentation and EDA: rapid reference, general data understanding, QA, validation and similar", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 12:39 CT; carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-A4@2", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:An undeclared question or intention can fall back", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D2", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "CHARTER.md (eight rules) is the engineering charter", "rationale": "carried from eraevous/Data-Guide (archived) DG-D2@1; only pointers changed on carrying it over", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Charter looks good, too", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "CHARTER.md", "sha256": "f82954a9027208d8efbaea290941cda8563703f98b76808eb9fbb91f259e7237", "locator": "q:Each rule gives: Rule", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "DG-D3", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "The April 2026 design is the starting architecture: Connector -> GuideDataFrame -> Profiler -> ProfilingResult -> Renderer, wide and long data models with a SchemaContract, an annotations slot for narratives, the MVP connectors and credential rules; distilled in docs/design.md, and overridden where later accepted records differ", "rationale": "The April design spec was marked Approved on 2026-04-20; that evidence is the spec's own status line in the archived repository, not a quote. Zach chose to distil rather than copy it on 2026-11-01", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/design.md", "sha256": "a1f08d2f3e477bff0aca1443b1ee8447f6f7300ab1cd594b0240c2727298aeea", "locator": "q:**Key principle:** every connector produces", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:The April design spec and plan: **Distil, don't copy.**", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D4", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "Fathom restarts Data Guide in a fresh public repository from its guiding documents and decisions only (no earlier code), and is built from them with AEC and Spec Kit by Codex working cold, to see how far a project gets from documents alone", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Blow it away.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:seeing what a \"from scratch\" repo built using AEC could get to", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01.md", "sha256": "12858ce540f73b13f4a2cad94c09a6bd978e19657115aac1bca533368246b332", "locator": "q:Who builds: **Codex, cold.**", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Deliver a CSV/wide data-to-decisions slice: evidenced review actions and unknowns, overridable inferred semantics, bounded target-selected relationships, versioned artifact with standalone reports and human working record, and context-first profile comparison. Scope is specs/001-data-review/spec.md; proposed for Zach to accept.", "rationale": "HO-20261101-004 authorizes implementation of provisional feature requirements. Narrower readings are in codex_++/intents/2026-11-01__data-review.intent.md.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RB@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RD@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RE@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RF@1"}]}
{"id": "FT-R1", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Deliver a CSV/wide data-to-decisions slice: evidenced review actions and unknowns, overridable inferred semantics, bounded target-selected relationships, versioned artifact with standalone reports and human working record, and context-first profile comparison. Scope is specs/001-data-review/spec.md; proposed for Zach to accept.", "rationale": "HO-20261101-004 authorizes implementation of provisional feature requirements. Narrower readings are in codex_++/intents/2026-11-01__data-review.intent.md.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RB@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RD@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RE@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RF@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-R1@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.connectors.CSVConnector.load"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.profile"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.select_pairs"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.compare"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.renderers.render_html"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.renderers.render_markdown"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:src.fathom.cli.main"}], "anchors": [{"path": "specs/001-data-review/spec.md", "sha256": "e8e04ff1daa48d4220a84d0369e33bf5bb1493f4b30cf65fcf07fe5c5521408d", "locator": "q:An analyst supplies a public or synthetic CSV", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "FT-C1", "version": 1, "type": "claim", "tier": "candidate", "claim_category": "requirement_satisfaction", "text": "The implementation conforms to the proposed FT-R1 slice on the tested synthetic scenarios: evidenced review actions and unknowns, inference overrides, bounded target pairs, saved reports, and context-first comparisons. This is not owner acceptance or a claim that the purpose outcome is achieved.", "relations": [{"rel": "implements", "to": "FT-R1@2"}]}
{"id": "FT-V1", "version": 1, "type": "evaluation", "text": "Examine the implemented data review contract with authored synthetic fixtures, clean decoys, hand-calculated summaries and subprocess byte comparisons.", "conditions": "Python 3.12.14; clean local venv; pandas 2.2.3, PyYAML 6.0.3, NumPy 2.5.4, pytest 9.2.0; core without SciPy, then SciPy 1.18.1. Details: specs/001-data-review/validation.md.", "relations": [{"rel": "tests", "to": "FT-C1@1"}, {"rel": "produced", "to": "FT-E1@1"}]}
{"id": "FT-E1", "version": 1, "type": "evidence", "tier": "candidate", "evidence_kind": "contract_conformance", "text": "Clean core install: 67 passed, 1 SciPy-present decoy skipped. With stats extra: 68 passed. Quickstart profile/render/compare/validate succeeds; fresh-process outputs match byte-for-byte. Dirty fixture has exactly two evidenced review actions; clean decoy has neither.", "method": "python -m pytest -q in clean core and stats environments; installed guide quickstart; exact exported byte comparisons.", "limits": "Machine-produced synthetic conformance evidence, not independent review, real-data usefulness, a purpose-outcome observation or Zach acceptance.", "relations": [{"rel": "supports", "to": "FT-C1@1"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.profile"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.select_pairs"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.profiler.compare"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.renderers.render_html"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.renderers.render_markdown"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:src.fathom.cli.main"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:tests.test_understanding.test_review_actions_and_clean_decoy"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:tests.test_cli.test_cli_roundtrip_compare_validate_and_reproducibility"}, {"rel": "observed_on", "to": "code:tests.test_pairs.test_missing_optional_dependency_degrades"}]}
// 2026-11-01: proposals after fathom-001 trial 1 (provisional; Zach accepts).
{"id": "FT-R2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "The MVP surfaces, as findings with evidence (not only as dictionary statistics), at least: sentinel or placeholder values (e.g. 999, -1 at a column's extreme); test or dummy values; dominant or near-constant columns; duplicate or lockstep columns; columns missing together on the same rows; missingness that varies with the target or another column; temporal coverage gaps; strong skew where it changes what a typical value means; and exact duplicate rows. Meanings stay labelled hypotheses or questions (DG-RB)", "rationale": "Proposed by claude:aec after fathom-001 trial 1 (2026-11-01): slice 1 turned 1 of 10 planted problems into a finding; Zach asked for these to be written up (15:21 CT: \"go ahead and write those up\"). Provisional until Zach accepts.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**Categorical:** counts and rates, entropy, dominance, rare levels, and dummy or test values.", "for": "text"}, {"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**Temporal:** coverage, gaps, volume patterns, trends and seasonality.", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "FT-R3", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Within the pair budget, candidate pairs are ranked by relevance to the declared question or target (e.g. strength of association, missingness linked to the target), not taken in column order; near-duplicate and near-constant columns don't consume the budget; the report states the ranking rule and what was excluded and why", "rationale": "Proposed by claude:aec after fathom-001 trial 1 (2026-11-01): slice 1 turned 1 of 10 planted problems into a finding; Zach asked for these to be written up (15:21 CT: \"go ahead and write those up\"). Provisional until Zach accepts. Slice 1 took pairs in column order, so a duplicate and a near-constant column used the budget while the column that leaks the target was excluded.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/vision.md", "sha256": "8e4998abab5e758b332e6de8fe30d299851543aa68a2b5bbb6cc47dc119d576a", "locator": "q:**C.** Let the analysis question", "for": "text"}]}
{"id": "FT-R4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "acceptance", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "A slice is judged useful by docs/acceptance.md: on a table it was not developed against, the report alone lets an analyst learn something consequential the raw table did not make obvious, without claiming more than it knows, and can serve as that table's standalone documentation. Builders check their own planted-problem tables and list found/missed in the PR", "rationale": "Proposed by claude:aec after fathom-001 trial 1 (2026-11-01): slice 1 turned 1 of 10 planted problems into a finding; Zach asked for these to be written up (15:21 CT: \"go ahead and write those up\"). Provisional until Zach accepts. The criterion was previously visible only to judges, not to the builder.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/acceptance.md", "sha256": "f6d38d6b8c246acfdaa20e0c92d7810e62b87e5b40452d733927265c76ac9c16", "locator": "q:can the analyst understand something consequential", "for": "text"}]}
// 2026-11-01 16:46 CT: Zach accepts FT-R2..R4, adds FT-R5 (summary), FT-R6 (readability) and the build order DG-D5.
