{"id": "FT-R3", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Within the pair budget, candidate pairs are ranked by relevance to the declared question or target (e.g. strength of association, missingness linked to the target), not taken in column order; near-duplicate and near-constant columns don't consume the budget; the report states the ranking rule and what was excluded and why", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 16:46 CT (\"pretty much correct\"); data-quality checks come first", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-R3@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:FTR2, R3, and R4 are all pretty much correct.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R4", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "acceptance", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "A slice is judged useful by docs/acceptance.md: on a table it was not developed against, the report alone lets an analyst learn something consequential the raw table did not make obvious, without claiming more than it knows, and can serve as that table's standalone documentation. Builders check their own planted-problem tables and list found/missed in the PR", "rationale": "Accepted by Zach 2026-11-01 16:46 CT (\"pretty much correct\"); data-quality checks come first", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-R4@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:FTR2, R3, and R4 are all pretty much correct.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R5", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The report opens with a dataset-level summary: rows and columns; complete rows (no missing cell) and complete columns (no missing value), as counts and shares; exact duplicate rows; duplicated or lockstep columns; columns by inferred type; constant and near-constant columns; and overall missing cells. Each figure links to the findings it supports", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 16:46 CT", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:How many rows were complete? How many columns were complete? How many columns were duplicated? How many columns of various types are there?", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R6", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The report is readable by a person first: it leads with what the data cannot tell and with usefulness, then findings grouped by kind (observations, interpretations, hypotheses, suggested actions, open questions) as one plain sentence each with its evidence a click away, then relations, then a compact per-column dictionary, then provenance. Repetitive per-column findings (e.g. one type and one meaning question per column) are summarised, not listed one by one", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-01 16:46 CT: slice 1's format is hard to read; he liked the structure of a reference report from an earlier prototype, described here in words (that report is not in this repository)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:The format is atrocious to read", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:I liked the format of guidereport.html.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D5", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "Build order: data-quality checks first (FT-R2 to FT-R5), with readability (FT-R6); then more advanced univariate analyses and visuals; then bivariate; then multivariate", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:That is what I would be interested in first, is data quality checks.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:For next steps, I would prefer some more advanced univariate analyses and visuals", "for": "rationale"}]}
// 2026-11-01 16:55 CT: FT-R6@2 (view switch), FT-R7 (target analyses), FT-R8 (switchable charts), DG-D5@2.
{"id": "FT-R6", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The report is readable by a person first: it leads with what the data cannot tell and with usefulness, then findings grouped by kind (observations, interpretations, hypotheses, suggested actions, open questions) as one plain sentence each with its evidence a click away, then relations, then a compact per-column dictionary, then provenance. Repetitive per-column findings (e.g. one type and one meaning question per column) are summarised, not listed one by one. The HTML offers a one-click switch between the summarised view and the full per-item detail, self-contained (inline script or native expand/collapse, no external assets); the summarised view is the default, and both views derive from the same artifact", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-01 16:46 CT: slice 1's format is hard to read; he liked the structure of a reference report from an earlier prototype, described here in words (that report is not in this repository)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-R6@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:The format is atrocious to read", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:I liked the format of guidereport.html.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:Is it possible to have that summarization piece clickable in the HTML", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R7", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "When a target (dependent variable) is declared, the report compares the target with each other column using light, type-appropriate measures of association or shared information (for example correlation, correlation ratio, Cramer's V, mutual information, target rates by group or bin), not a fitted model per column; it ranks columns by that relationship and labels every measure as descriptive, not causal. Target-versus-pairs of columns comes later. Model-based comparisons, if any, are opt-in", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 16:55 CT as an addendum to DG-D5. The measures listed are examples; a spec chooses them", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:I would also like target-based analyses.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:I don't want every bivariate comparison to run like a logistic regression", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:and also eventually we'll want target versus bivariate.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R8", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Where it saves room, charts are switchable in the self-contained HTML: the reader picks the variable on the x axis and on the y axis (or the column shown) from controls, instead of the report printing one chart per combination. The choices offered stay within what the question and the budget selected (DG-RC), and the static Markdown keeps a non-interactive fallback", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 16:55 CT, after a Power BI report he configured with click-to-change axes", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:could be clicked to change to other variables", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D5", "version": 2, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "Build order: data-quality checks first (FT-R2 to FT-R5), with readability (FT-R6); then more advanced univariate analyses and visuals; then bivariate and multivariate, including target-based analyses (FT-R7: target versus each column, later target versus pairs) and switchable charts (FT-R8)", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:That is what I would be interested in first, is data quality checks.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening.md", "sha256": "2b72ad6573419840163bae048f099578592b43838f3f63e43fd9d8f516bbbab8", "locator": "q:For next steps, I would prefer some more advanced univariate analyses and visuals", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:Addendum to DGD5.", "for": "rationale"}], "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "DG-D5@1"}]}
